    {
      "filename": "DSC00032 Java Ouest Little Village Kampung Naga (6220092346).jpg",
      "title": "File:DSC00032 Java Ouest Little Village Kampung Naga (6220092346).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1b/DSC00032_Java_Ouest_Little_Village_Kampung_Naga_%286220092346%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DSC00032_Java_Ouest_Little_Village_Kampung_Naga_(6220092346).jpg",
      "width": 2256,
      "height": 1504,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "DANIEL JULIE from Paris, France",
      "description": "The little traditional village named Kampung Naga is situated Java West , near the vilage of Neglasari and city of Tasikmalaya . This area is mainly used for rice production with 3 harvest by year because the climatic condition are particularly good and auspicious.\n\nKampung Naga is a village which is inhabited by a community in a very strong tradition of holding the remainder ancestors. The differences are visible when compared with other communities outside Kampung Naga. The community are living in the framework of an atmosphere in a traditional simplicity and environmental wisdom.",
      "dateCreated": "2011-09-07 08:38",
